hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"28167","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Ubaydullah ibn Abi Rafi, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his mother Salma, she said: Fatimah complained of her complaint in which she died, and I used to nurse her. One morning she became as well as I ever saw her in that complaint. She said: And Ali went out for some need, and she said: O mother, pour for me a wash, and I poured for her a wash, and she washed as well as I ever saw her wash. Then she said: O mother, give me my new clothes, and I gave her and she wore them. Then she said: O mother, bring forward my bed to the middle of the house, and I did, and she lay down and faced the qiblah and placed her hand under her cheek, then she said: O mother, I am taken now, I am taken now, and I have purified myself, so let no one uncover me. She died in her place. She said: Ali came and I informed him."
"28168","Abdullah said: Muhammad ibn Jafar al-Warakani narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ishaq, and he mentioned the like of it, the same."
